{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"dfc8ea9956785d10","name":"card_event_hasty_reinforcements","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/WorldAtWar/events/card_event_hasty_reinforcements","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HASTY REINFORCEMENTS","text":"Units you deploy or add this turn randomly get +1+1, Blitz or Ambush.","flavorText":"During WWII the Red Army grew extensively and by the war's end around 30 million Soviet men and women had been drafted to military service. Prior to the war the Soviet Union did not have a comprehensive military draft so many of the people that were drafted during WWII had no military experience. In general most recruits spent 3 months in training and were properly prepared when they reached the frontlines. However, in Oct-Nov 1941 the training of many units was cut short due to the lack of manpower. Most fresh recruits were distributed among more seasoned troops in the frontlines where they finished their training. In these cases the training was mostly about surviving the first 3 attacks, which is the most critical period for fresh recruits. ","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_hasty_reinforcements","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_hasty_reinforcements_title","SourceString":"HASTY REINFORCEMENTS","LocalizedString":"HASTY REINFORCEMENTS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_hasty_reinforcements_text","SourceString":"Units you deploy or add this turn randomly get +1+1, Blitz or Ambush.","LocalizedString":"Units you deploy or add this turn randomly get +1+1, Blitz or Ambush."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_hasty_reinforcements_history","SourceString":"During WWII the Red Army grew extensively and by the war's end around 30 million Soviet men and women had been drafted to military service. Prior to the war the Soviet Union did not have a comprehensive military draft so many of the people that were drafted during WWII had no military experience. In general most recruits spent 3 months in training and were properly prepared when they reached the frontlines. However, in Oct-Nov 1941 the training of many units was cut short due to the lack of manpower. Most fresh recruits were distributed among more seasoned troops in the frontlines where they finished their training. In these cases the training was mostly about surviving the first 3 attacks, which is the most critical period for fresh recruits. ","LocalizedString":"During WWII the Red Army grew extensively and by the war's end around 30 million Soviet men and women had been drafted to military service. Prior to the war the Soviet Union did not have a comprehensive military draft so many of the people that were drafted during WWII had no military experience. In general most recruits spent 3 months in training and were properly prepared when they reached the frontlines. However, in Oct-Nov 1941 the training of many units was cut short due to the lack of manpower. Most fresh recruits were distributed among more seasoned troops in the frontlines where they finished their training. In these cases the training was mostly about surviving the first 3 attacks, which is the most critical period for fresh recruits. "},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'October_Red'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/October_Red.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/CandidateArtwork/t_hasty_reinforcements.t_hasty_reinforcements","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Soviet WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/HASTY_REINFORCEMENTS.HASTY_REINFORCEMENTS","SubPa